  SPDX-FileCopyrightText: Copyright (c) 2026 newmassrael

  The relay of shared lists as a firewalld service (docs/SCE_RELAY_DEPLOY.md), installed as
  /etc/firewalld/services/sce-relay.xml and added to the zone the server faces the network in:

    firewall-cmd --reload
    firewall-cmd --permanent --zone=public --add-service=sce-relay
    firewall-cmd --reload

  The port is the one the relay listens on with TLS ([listen] tls in relay.toml). A relay behind a
  proxy on the same server opens no port of its own: the proxy's port is opened instead.
-->
<service>
  <short>sce-relay</short>
  <description>The relay of shared lists: its WebSocket binding over TLS (wss://).</description>
  <port protocol="tcp" port="443"/>
</service>
